Package: Pando
Version: 2.0.1
Type: Package
Title: Inferring regulomes from multi-modal single-cell genomics data
Authors@R: person(given = "Jonas Simon",
               family = "Fleck",
               role = c("aut", "cre"),
               email = "jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch",
               comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4686-7254"))
Maintainer: Jonas Simon Fleck <jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch>
Description: Pando jointly uses scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq measurements to infer
    regulatory relationships between TF-binding site pairs and target genes.
    For two or more conditions within a broad cell type, infer_condition_grn
    uses one canonical two-stage procedure. Candidate edges are discovered on
    the complete cell type and separately in each condition using the original
    Pando peak-to-gene, motif, peak-target-correlation and TF-target-correlation
    steps. Exact TF-peak-target triples are unioned into one frozen dictionary.
    Every condition is then refitted with the same Gaussian identity Pando
    interaction model, the same predictor columns and the same globally
    preprocessed RNA and ATAC layers, with scale set to FALSE. The selected
    layers, peak-value semantics and a stable preprocessing fingerprint are
    stored in every condition fit and verified again during projection.
    Condition effects are the resulting coefficients; no pooled-coefficient
    calibration is applied. Coefficients retain standard errors, P values and
    network-wide adjusted P values. Only adjusted-P values below the configured
    threshold enter the exported penalty effect, while the complete coefficient
    table is retained for audit. Zero-variance and aliased edges remain
    unavailable rather than being silently converted to fitted zeros. When no
    condition column is supplied, the column is absent, or fewer than two levels
    are observed, the original per-cell-type infer_grn Gaussian interaction
    workflow is used and no condition coefficient is created. Independent
    cell-type jobs can be dispatched through BiocParallel without nested worker
    pools, and condition-only controls are removed before standard infer_grn
    model arguments are forwarded to regression backends.
